Making a variable: name=kai

Unsetting a variable:
 - name=
 - unset name

uname command shows system name
uname -a shows more system info (everything in uname)

Use backticks to store the output of a command in a variable
 - myMachine=`uname -a`

Backticks work but are old syntax. New syntax is to use $()
 - myMachine=$(uname -a)

